   "text": {
    "L1": "Equivalent fractions name the same amount with different-sized parts.",
    "L2": "Adding the same number to the top and bottom does not keep a fraction equal. One-half is not two-thirds.",
    "L3": "To make an equivalent fraction, multiply the numerator and denominator by the same number.",
    "L4": "Cutting each part into two gives twice as many parts, each half as large. So one-half becomes two-fourths.",
    "L5": "The same idea gives three-sixths. One-half, two-fourths, and three-sixths name the same amount.",
    "L6": "To reduce a fraction, divide the top and bottom by a common factor.",
    "L7": "For eighteen over twenty-four, divide both by two, then both by three. The lowest terms are three-fourths.",
    "L8": "Now use the rule: choose the fraction that names the same amount as one-half."
   },
